cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fesom_kokkos: a C++/Kokkos port of the FESOM2 ocean and sea-ice model for CPUs and GPUs"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it, together with the FESOM2 model it ports."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Koldunov
    given-names: Nikolay
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3365-8146"
    affiliation: Alfred Wegener Institute, Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research
  - family-names: Beyer
    given-names: Sebastian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3731-0278"
    affiliation: Alfred Wegener Institute, Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research
version: 1.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/koldunovn/fesom_kokkos"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  A performance-portable C++/Kokkos port of the ocean and sea-ice core of the
  FESOM2 unstructured-mesh model. One source tree builds for CPUs (Kokkos Serial
  and OpenMP back-ends) and GPUs (CUDA and HIP). The Serial build reproduces the C
  port (fesom_port) byte for byte; the GPU builds keep the whole time step on the
  device and exchange halos with GPU-aware MPI.
keywords:
  - ocean model
  - sea ice
  - FESOM2
  - Kokkos
  - GPU
  - performance portability
